  m_text: "Sunspots are dark, cooler regions on the Sun\u2019s photosphere caused
    by intense magnetic activity. They appear darker because they are cooler than
    the surrounding areas, but they are still extremely hot. Sunspots often occur
    in pairs or groups and can last from days to weeks. They are indicators of solar
    activity and are closely linked to solar flares and coronal mass ejections."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c1a6766cc90ee6042bda611a62866980, type: 2}
